course: dictionary
lesson: 12103
title: Cohabit: living together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To cohabit means to live together. Look at its parts: «co-» means together, and «habit» comes from a word meaning to live or dwell. Those clues help you guess the meaning before you check.
explain: «Sam and Priya decided to cohabit before they got married.» Sam and Priya live together in one home as a couple, but they are not married yet. Cohabit is a formal word, so you will see it mostly in official papers and serious writing.
explain: The word can also mean living or existing together in the same place. «Many species cohabit in the rainforest.» No couple is involved here: lots of different animals and plants share one habitat. Look at the words around cohabit to tell which meaning the writer means.
explain: In everyday talk, people usually say «live together» instead. To check, swap that phrase into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Cohabit means to live together.
fact: «Co-» means together, and «habit» comes from a word meaning to live or dwell.
fact: Meaning one: a couple living together in one home without being married.
fact: Meaning two: different animals or plants living together in the same place, such as a habitat.
fact: Cohabit is a formal word; «live together» is the everyday way to say it.
exercise: «Sam and Priya chose to cohabit in a flat before their wedding.» What does cohabit mean here? | To get married in a big church | To argue loudly about money | *To live together as a couple, not married | To move house every year
exercise: «Many species cohabit in the rainforest.» What does cohabit mean in this sentence? | To hide from other animals | To cut down the trees | To fly far away | *To live together in the same place
exercise: Which everyday phrase means the same as cohabit? | Sleep alone | *Live together | Fall apart | Go on holiday
test: «The two cats cohabit happily in the same garden.» Cohabit here means what? | Run away from home | *Live together in the same place | Argue all day | Sleep in separate houses
test: Which word is the best synonym for cohabit? | Divide | Travel | *Share a home | Forget
exam: Which part of «cohabit» means together? | habit | *co- | -bit | -ate
